# --> CSS GRID
* display
* grid-templete-columns
* grid-templete-rows
* gap
* repeat()
* grid-area
* line-based placement/grid-lines
* grid-templete-area
* units
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Note: Margin: Auto and Grid
When you set margin: auto on a grid item, it will center itself within the grid cell both horizontally and vertically. This is because the auto value for margin allows the item to take up any remaining space in the grid cell, effectively centering it.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Responsive Web Design 
Responsive web design is an approach to web development that aims to create websites that provide an optimal viewing experience across a wide range of devices, from desktop computers to mobile phones. The goal of responsive web design is to ensure that a website's layout and content adapt seamlessly to different screen sizes and orientations, providing users with a consistent and user-friendly experience regardless of the device they are using.

---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
# --> CSS Positioning
* position: static
* position: relative
* position: absolute:
   1. take space only based on the its content and its size.
   2. position itself based on the nearest positioned ancestor (relative, absolute, fixed, or sticky).
* position: fixed
* position: sticky
